   modelled as a surface deformable tube with a closed toe and an open cuff. The task reuses the
   observations, actions, commands, terminations, and curriculum of ``Isaac-Lift-Cloth-Franka``, and
   drops that task's support rails because the tube keeps a graspable cross-section on its own.
+
+Changed
+^^^^^^^
+
+* Improved the rendering of ``IsaacContrib-Lift-Sock-Franka``:
+
+  * The divider walls now span from the floor to 1 m above the table (previously just the 0.6 m
+    above the table top), and each environment draws a different NVIDIA Nucleus MDL material on
+    its walls through heterogeneous cloning, rather than the Replicator-based texture-randomization
+    events, which require ``replicate_physics=False`` and are unsupported on the Newton backend
+    this task defaults to.
+  * The table and ground now show PBR materials (wood and polished concrete) instead of being
+    invisible/checker-textured; success is now shown by a small marker disc on a table corner
+    instead of tinting the whole table, since the table is no longer invisible.
+  * Added a directional light alongside the existing dome light, and switched the dome light to a
+    partly-cloudy sky, for more defined shadows.
+  * The sock's bending stiffness (``edge_ke``) is reduced from 30 to 2 so it drapes and folds like
+    fabric instead of holding a rigid tube shape, with the mesh resolution raised from 20 to 28
+    segments to keep the folds smooth. ``SOCK_RESTING_HEIGHT`` (and the reward's lift threshold
+    derived from it) is updated to match the flatter settled shape this produces.
